; galena-dns local blocklist (RPZ)
;
; Loaded SECOND: after the allowlist, ahead of every downloaded feed. The
; allowlist stays first so that a false positive in here is overridden exactly
; the way one in any other zone is — `make audit` asserts that ordering.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Why this zone exists when Quad9 already blocks most of what is in it
;
; Quad9 denies a blocked name with an UNSIGNED NXDOMAIN. For a signed parent
; zone our local validator correctly refuses that forged denial, so the client
; sees SERVFAIL rather than NXDOMAIN. The name is still blocked — but some
; clients retry SERVFAIL against a fallback resolver, which both defeats the
; block and sends that query somewhere else. A name listed HERE is answered
; locally by RPZ, and RPZ rewrites are not validated against the real zone, so
; it returns a clean NXDOMAIN and the query never leaves the node.
; See README, "Two things measured after the switch".
;
; Measured 2026-10-16 from a node, against 9.9.9.9 over DoT:
;
;     fearevolve.com         NXDOMAIN, AUTHORITY: 0   no SOA, no NSEC3, no RRSIG
;     zq7x4-...-nope.com     NXDOMAIN, AUTHORITY: 8   full signed denial
;
; and through our own unbound: SERVFAIL when validating, NXDOMAIN with +cd.
; That is the forged-denial path confirmed, not assumed.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Owner names are RELATIVE to the zone apex, exactly as in allowlist.rpz: a
; bare "example.com" below blocks example.com. No trailing dot. The wildcard is
; listed separately because it does NOT cover the bare name.
;
;     example.com            CNAME .
;     *.example.com          CNAME .
;
; After editing, `make deploy`. To check it took effect:
;     unbound-control auth_zone_reload blocklist.rpz.galena
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

$TTL 3600
@   SOA localhost. root.localhost. 1 3600 600 86400 3600
@   NS  localhost.

; --- Citizen Lab Report 195, "Exposing AdFection", 2026-10-15 ---------------
;
; Candiru (trading as Integrity Labs) validator and C&C infrastructure, plus one
; Discover-Tech-linked domain that behaves identically. Added 2026-10-16.
;
; These are the AdFection indicators that no local feed carries. Checked against
; Hagezi pro, tif.mini and tif-ips as deployed on 2026-10-16: all nine were
; absent from all three, and blocked upstream only. The Discover-Tech ad
; DELIVERY domains from the same report — mtrtb.com, controlium.net and 15 more
; — are deliberately not repeated here, because Hagezi pro already carries them
; and they already answer as a clean local NXDOMAIN. Verified, not assumed.
;
; All nine were already dead at the registry when they were added, so this is a
; guard against re-registration and rotation, not a live block.

; Validators
keyadapter.com             CNAME .
*.keyadapter.com           CNAME .
sharethere.net             CNAME .
*.sharethere.net           CNAME .

; Command and control
fearevolve.com             CNAME .
*.fearevolve.com           CNAME .
jobmarcher.com             CNAME .
*.jobmarcher.com           CNAME .
insightenterprisells.com   CNAME .
*.insightenterprisells.com CNAME .
plasticbells.com           CNAME .
*.plasticbells.com         CNAME .
outdooutcome.com           CNAME .
*.outdooutcome.com         CNAME .
suggestutterly.com         CNAME .
*.suggestutterly.com       CNAME .

; Discover-Tech linked, same forged-denial behaviour as the C&C set
sincereaccertain.com       CNAME .
*.sincereaccertain.com     CNAME .

